This report presents the initial observation of the $B^0_s\to\bar{D}^0 K^0_S$ decay mode and provides evidence for the $B^0_s\to\bar{D}^{*0} K^0_S$ process. The analysis is based on $3.0\,\text{fb}^{-1}$ of integrated luminosity from $pp$ collisions at $\sqrt{s}=7$ and $8\,\text{TeV}$, collected by the LHCb experiment. The measured branching fractions are given as
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{B}(B^0_s\to\bar{D}^{0} K^0_S) & = (4.4\,\pm\,0.7\,\pm\,0.4\,(\text{stat})\,\pm\,0.7\,(\text{sys}))\times 10^{-5}, \\
\mathcal{B}(B^0_s\to\bar{D}^{*0} K^0_S) & = (5.8\,\pm\,0.9\,\pm\,0.5\,(\text{stat})\,\pm\,1.0\,(\text{sys}))\times 10^{-5}.
\end{align*}
